 here  together  one analyst says the causes of the  unrest run deep  towns and cities that have once been  pretty much peaceful  bastions of coexistence are now blowing  up with  direct hand-to-hand combat what i would  say is that there's an ongoing  systemic issue of oppression of  palestinian  citizens diplomatic efforts have so far  achieved little they want to see  de-escalation they want to see both  sides  sitting down talking through and  stopping the violence  what we do mean now is diplomacy this is  the incredibly  sad thing while politics is being played  and missiles are being thrown back and  forth there are people on the ground  children mothers fathers on both sides  being killed  israel's prime minister elbow-bumped  israeli soldiers today  he said we continue striking hamas and  added it will  take more time it's clear now what  netanyahu meant as troops gathered on  the gaza border  and late thursday night israel sent its  military into gaza  eric sorensen global news toronto  the garretts and the michaels still  ahead the links between two stories of  canadians detained in china  global news is launching a new series  called china rising the podcast will  examine how the chinese government is  allegedly targeting canada and its  allies  deploying a range of tactics including  hostage diplomacy  the most famous examples of canadians  being held in china are of course  michael spavor and michael kovrig  but they aren't the only canadians who  have been caught in the political  crossfire  jeff semple spoke to julia and kevin  garrett about their experience  and their advice to others  for nearly two and a half years the two  michaels have remained  out of reach canadian spavor and kovrig  accused by beijing of spying their  trials held behind  closed doors their ordeal difficult to  even imagine  but not for julia and kevin garrett our  situation is very similar to the  michaels  the canadian couple lived in china for  three decades before their arrest in  2014  accused of spying following the arrest  of a chinese suspect  in canada at the request of the united  states the garretts were held in  separate cells  interrogated for six hours every day  they threatened execution many times  they each kept diaries in john 15.  kevin wrote bible verses about hope  while julia scribbled pictures of  anything she was grateful for  like i heard a bird outside i heard like  some chirping of a bird so i drew like a  few birds  because the other alternative is you get  lost in  bitterness anger rage and i knew that  wasn't a good choice but as the months  dragged on  their notes grew darker like you get  into this more  deep deep despair after seven months  julia was released  but not kevin like the michaels his  trial was also closed to the public  which he believes is actually a positive  if it was a public trial meaning there  are spectators  it will not go away they're going to  make an example of you  kevin was later convicted of spying but  unbeknownst to him  political relations were warming the  chinese suspect in canada  suddenly pleaded guilty and prime  minister trudeau visited  china amid talk of a possible trade deal  two weeks later kevin was released  reunited with his family  the garretts say the government's quiet  backdoor diplomacy  helped to secure their release so their  approach was  extremely diplomatic and so it wasn't in  the media  they're doing it differently with the  two michaels uh some quiet action but  more  in the news and in in their face but  even when it seems  insurmountable their story is a reminder  of how quickly the winds  can change i think i would say you hold  on  it will not last forever jeff semple  global news toronto  you can listen to china rising on apple  podcast spotify  amazon music or wherever you get your  favorite podcasts  a jab for the jackpot next some million  dollar incentives to get vaccinated  you can get a vaccine at the game  new york governor andrew cuomo is  offering a perk for baseball fans get  vaccinated at clinics set up at mets and  yankees games and you not only get  protected you'll get a free ticket to  another game most americans under the  age of 65 are not vaccinated yet and  there's a big push on to fix that  easing the rules about masks for fully  vaccinated americans is one incentive  jackson proskow explains some others  did you say free fries when you get  vaccinated  i got vaccinated from free burgers and  fries to donuts and beer there you go  the push to encourage vaccination has  turned into a personalized sales pitch  anything we can do to get the jabs in  people's arms i think is great  so some states are paying people to get  the vaccine  50 dollars in parts of texas 100 savings  bonds in west virginia  and then there's ohio where you can get  a shot and win a lot  that first number up tonight is seven  five one million dollar prizes  in a special lottery for the fully  vaccinated you have the other group of  people though  who are not vaccinated and the danger to  them is even more  great in some respects than it has been  in the past because this variant  is more contagious canadians are getting  a taste of it  even if they can't yet get their second  shots montreal-based acom  timber will pay employees 350  once they're fully vaccinated the  university of lethbridge is giving away  free tuition to nine students who get  their first shot by september  we are very committed to doing  everything we can  to make sure that we create a safe and  healthy environment  in the fall and vaccinations are part of  that  you don't address vaccine hesitancy by  buying compliance  some epidemiologists question the ethics  of it all believing social incentives  promoting a return to normal  are better get vaccinated you can do all  these wonderful things like hug your  loved ones and be in your room  without math and go to the theater et  cetera and when the toronto blue jays  play their  home opener in buffalo new york fans  will get a grand slam of that kind of  encouragement  a special section without distancing for  the fully vaccinated  and free shots in the stadium for those  who still need them  jackson proskow global news washington  and that is global national for this  thursday i'll say goodbye tonight  wishing eid mubarak to muslims in canada  and around the world who are celebrating  the end of the holy month of ramadan  we leave you tonight with some images of  eid prayers and  celebrations from around the globe  thanks for watching
 

